  {
   "text": "Welcome to the Dementia Services section\nCaring for a person living with dementia can be challenging. It can affect your emotions, your health, your time, and your finances. You are not alone - many services are available to support you and your family. \nThis section helps you find dementia-related services near you in a simple way. \nTo get started: \r\nThe map will automatically show services near the address in your profile\nIf you want to search in a different area, type a new address into the “Search location” box\nYou can choose different types of services (for example, hospitals, respite care, or peer support)  \r\nYou can also adjust how far from your location you would like to search\nDementia care often requires different types of support. Services you may find helpful include:\nGovernment-funded aged care services\nDisability support services (for people diagnosed before age 65)\nCarer support, including counselling and peer support\nHelp to support your loved one at home\nSpecialist services for managing behaviour changes\nRespite care, so you can take a break\nWe understand that language and cultural needs are important. Some services may offer interpreters or culturally appropriate  care - please check with the service provider.   For more information about support services, please see Module 6 in the iSupport course. ",
